1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:04,417
The Audit Trail keeps a copy of a content item each time it

2
00:00:04,417 --> 00:00:06,940
changes, for the content types you choose.

3
00:00:06,940 --> 00:00:10,778
In this video, you open an earlier version, compare it with the one

4
00:00:10,778 --> 00:00:14,300
before it, and restore an earlier version and a deleted item.

5
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:23,550
The Audit Trail records an event each time a content item is created,

6
00:00:23,550 --> 00:00:27,580
saved, published, unpublished, removed, cloned or restored.

7
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:31,424
Each event keeps a full copy of the item as it was, with

8
00:00:31,424 --> 00:00:33,160
the user and the time.

9
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:37,379
From a copy, you can view the item as it was and compare

10
00:00:37,379 --> 00:00:39,674
it with the previous recorded copy.

11
00:00:39,674 --> 00:00:43,647
Where a Restore button appears, you can restore it as a draft, so

12
00:00:43,647 --> 00:00:47,060
the published page stays the same until you publish it.

13
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:51,359
Only the content types you choose in the settings are recorded.

14
00:00:51,359 --> 00:00:55,576
Events are removed after the retention period, which is ten days by default,

15
00:00:55,576 --> 00:00:57,788
unless you disable the trimming task.

16
00:00:57,788 --> 00:01:02,160
Restore appears on Published and Removed events, except for the latest version.

17
00:01:02,910 --> 00:01:06,350
Opening the Audit Trail needs the View audit trail permission.

18
00:01:06,350 --> 00:01:10,498
Viewing a version needs permission to edit the item, and restoring a version

19
00:01:10,498 --> 00:01:12,370
needs permission to publish it.

20
00:01:16,608 --> 00:01:22,293
With the Audit Trail feature enabled, open Settings, Audit Trail, and select the Content tab.

21
00:01:22,293 --> 00:01:27,462
Under Allowed content types, you choose which content types the Audit Trail records.

22
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:31,368
Until you choose at least one, no content events are recorded.

23
00:01:31,843 --> 00:01:33,890
Select Article, and click Save.

24
00:01:33,890 --> 00:01:37,098
Changes to articles are recorded from this point on.

25
00:01:37,098 --> 00:01:39,643
Changes made earlier are not in the log.

26
00:01:43,855 --> 00:01:47,935
In Content, Content Items, each item has an Actions menu.

27
00:01:47,935 --> 00:01:53,505
For the article Harvest Festival Cancelled, open Actions and choose Audit Trail.

28
00:01:53,979 --> 00:01:57,629
The list shows the events of this one item, newest first.

29
00:01:57,629 --> 00:02:02,379
Each line gives the event, its category, when it happened, who triggered it,

30
00:02:02,379 --> 00:02:04,349
and the version it concerns.

31
00:02:08,599 --> 00:02:12,179
Find the line of an earlier Published event, and click View.

32
00:02:13,187 --> 00:02:18,240
The article opens in a read-only editor, filled with the values it had in that version.

33
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:22,477
The page title names the content type, the title and the version number.

34
00:02:26,713 --> 00:02:30,582
Back in the list, click Details on the newest Published line.

35
00:02:30,582 --> 00:02:35,029
The page shows who triggered the event and when, then the type, display

36
00:02:35,029 --> 00:02:37,513
text and version of the content item.

37
00:02:37,965 --> 00:02:39,406
Select the Diff tab.

38
00:02:39,406 --> 00:02:44,284
The left side holds the previous recorded copy, and the right side holds this one.

39
00:02:44,284 --> 00:02:48,165
Changed lines are shaded red on the left and green on the right.

40
00:02:48,616 --> 00:02:51,848
Choose Unified to read both copies in one column.

41
00:02:51,848 --> 00:02:56,373
Some lines, such as the modified time, differ in every version, so look

42
00:02:56,373 --> 00:02:58,254
for the fields you edited:

43
00:02:58,254 --> 00:03:00,546
here, the title and the subtitle.

44
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:08,022
To undo the change, go back to the list and click Restore on

45
00:03:08,022 --> 00:03:10,856
the line of the earlier Published version you want.

46
00:03:10,856 --> 00:03:13,790
The line of the newest version has no Restore button.

47
00:03:14,247 --> 00:03:19,405
A dialog titled Restore to Version asks you to confirm the version number.

48
00:03:19,405 --> 00:03:20,437
Click Yes.

49
00:03:20,890 --> 00:03:25,595
The Audit Trail reports that the article has been restored, and a Restored

50
00:03:25,595 --> 00:03:27,183
event heads the list.

51
00:03:27,183 --> 00:03:31,830
The published page is unchanged, because the restored version is a draft.

52
00:03:32,285 --> 00:03:37,016
In Content Items, the article shows both a Published and a Draft status.

53
00:03:37,016 --> 00:03:42,535
Open Actions and choose Publish Draft to make the restored version the published one.

54
00:03:46,722 --> 00:03:51,048
Suppose the article Summer Parking Notice is deleted by mistake.

55
00:03:51,048 --> 00:03:55,806
In Content Items, open Actions, choose Delete, and click Ok to confirm.

56
00:03:55,806 --> 00:03:58,462
The article disappears from the list.

57
00:03:58,966 --> 00:04:00,523
Its history remains.

58
00:04:00,523 --> 00:04:02,319
Open Tools, Audit Trail:

59
00:04:02,319 --> 00:04:06,870
the deletion is recorded as a Removed event, and the event still holds

60
00:04:06,870 --> 00:04:08,546
a copy of the article.

61
00:04:09,006 --> 00:04:11,287
Click Restore on the Removed line.

62
00:04:11,287 --> 00:04:14,024
The dialog is titled Restore content item.

63
00:04:14,024 --> 00:04:14,936
Click Yes.

64
00:04:15,390 --> 00:04:19,826
The article returns to Content Items with the Draft status only, because a

65
00:04:19,826 --> 00:04:24,206
restore creates a draft and a deleted item has no published version left.

66
00:04:24,206 --> 00:04:27,200
Choose Publish Draft to put it back on the site.

67
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:31,340
That's the Audit Trail for content:

68
00:04:31,340 --> 00:04:35,723
you can view and compare recorded versions, and restore a published version or

69
00:04:35,723 --> 00:04:37,393
a deleted item as a draft.

70
00:04:37,393 --> 00:04:38,750
Thanks for watching.

